{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nGerrit Verified on GitHub Actions is now frequently 30–40 minutes, roughly double the prior 15–20 minute duration. The recent mutation-testing addition is a lead, not a conclusion. Prior work on baseborn-subtle-cricket, crushable-choosable-llama, and coercive-paediatric-bug measured earlier critical paths and org-wide runner contention; this investigation must distinguish execution time from queue time and must not re-propose rejected runner parallelism that leaves total runner usage unchanged.\n\n## Plan\n- Build a dated evidence dossier from current and historical gerrit-verify runs, job and step timings, workflow history, and the prior CI-latency tickets.\n- Identify the good-to-bad transition and quantify mutation testing contribution using comparable runs or a controlled local/CI experiment.\n- Generate falsifiable rival hypotheses and run discriminating experiments, including runtime evidence for dynamic causes.\n- Record a cited root cause and reference existing tickets for every remediation to prove whether it is new, accepted, completed, or previously rejected.\n- If existing telemetry is insufficient, add the smallest assurance-neutral observability needed, validate it, and land it through Gerrit before concluding.\n- Propose wall-clock reductions that preserve coverage and do not rely on increasing parallel jobs or unchanged aggregate runner consumption.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The current 30–40 minute symptom is decomposed into workflow queue time, job queue time, and execution critical path across a representative run sample.\n- [x] The good-to-bad transition is identified with dated workflow or commit evidence.\n- [x] Mutation testing has a specific measured wall-clock and runner-time contribution, including comparable before and after evidence.\n- [x] Rival hypotheses are confirmed or rejected by falsifiable experiments, with dynamic claims supported by runtime evidence.\n- [x] The proven root cause is recorded with repository, run, and ticket citations.\n- [x] Every proposed remediation references searched tracker history and states whether it is new, completed, accepted, or previously rejected.\n- [x] Recommendations preserve CI coverage and avoid parallelism that does not reduce aggregate runner usage.\n- [x] Any required observability change passes repository gates, Gerrit LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, and is merged before this ticket closes. No observability change was required: existing --durations=25 logs contained the necessary per-test evidence."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786599656621547001,"uuid":"b5014f8a-0a20-4916-b9e3-95b5bfdbe011"}